# Day 26

## Experiment Title

Deploying a Web Application using Docker Compose


## Objective

To deploy a simple web application using Docker Compose and understand service deployment in a containerized environment.


## Theory

Docker Compose can be used to deploy complete web applications by defining all required services in a single configuration file. A web application may contain multiple components such as a web server, backend service, and database.

Docker Compose simplifies application deployment by automatically creating containers, networks, and service communication. It allows applications to be deployed quickly and consistently across different systems.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and ensure that Docker services are running properly.

Create a Docker Compose configuration file for the web application.

Configure the web server image and required ports.

Start the application using Docker Compose.

Verify that the web application is running successfully in the browser.

Inspect the running containers from Docker Desktop.


## Output

The web application was deployed successfully using Docker Compose.

Containers were created and executed properly.

The application was accessible through the configured browser port.


## Result

Successfully deployed a web application using Docker Compose and understood the process of containerized application deployment.
